ld-commentary/biodiversity-un-synergies/</a></li><li>Gupta, H. (2023). Advancing youth climate action from global to local levels. Diplomatic Courier. <a href=\"https://www.diplomaticourier.com/posts/youth-climate-action-global-local\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.diplomaticourier.com/posts/youth-climate-action-global-local</a></li></ul>"},{"slug":"political-ideologies-and-their-perspectives-on-human-rights","html":"<ul><li>Baldi, Giorgia (2021), Re-Thinking Islam and Islamism: Hamas women between religion, secularism, and neo-liberalism. Middle East Critique, 31.1, pp. 1-22.</li><li>Baldi, Giorgia (2018) Between patriarchy and occupation: violence against women in the Occupied Palestinian Territories.In: Picelli, Giovanni, Borroni, Andrea and Kherkerulidze, Irine (eds.) Reconsidering gender based violence and other forms of violence against women: Comparative analysis in the light of the Istanbul Convention. Libellula University Press, Italy, pp. 247-295.</li><li>Baldi, Giorgia (2017) 'Burqa avenger': law and religious practices in secular space. Law and Critique, 29 (1). pp. 31-56.</li><li>Baldi, Giorgia (2016) Liberal paradoxes: women’s body, religious expression, and gender equality in a secular age. AG AboutGender, 5 (10). pp. 166-185.</li></ul>"},{"slug":"human-rights-violations-and-advocacy","html":"<ul><li>Martinez, M. (2023). Does the Inter-American Court of Human Rights affect the development of human rights norms in El Salvador, Honduras and Guatemala? International Studies, 60(1), 91-112.</li><li>Walker, L. D., Martinez, M., &amp; Pace, C. (2021). Gender, internal armed conflict, and High Court Decision-Making in transitioning societies. International Studies Quarterly, 65(3), 782–797. </li><li>Ishiyama, J., Martinez, M., &amp; Ozsut, M. (2018). Do “Resource-Cursed States” Have Lower Levels of Social and Institutional Trust? Evidence from Africa and Latin America. Social Science Quarterly, 99(3), 872–894.</li></ul>"},{"slug":"international-humanitarian-law-and-the-conduct-of-war","html":"<ul><li>Jegede, F. (2021). Doing a PhD in the Social Sciences: A student’s guide to post-graduate research and writing. Routledge.</li><li>Jegede, F., Hargreaves, C., Smith, K., Hodgson, P., Todd, M. J., &amp; Waldman, J. (2020). Writing successful undergraduate dissertations in Social Sciences A Student’s handbook. Routledge, Taylor &amp; Francis Group.</li><li>Jegede, F., Bampton, K., &amp; Todd, M. (2015, January). State vs non-state armed groups-a political economy of violence. In Annual International Conference Proceedings of the 5th Political Science, Sociology and International Relations (PSSIR 2015).</li></ul>"}]$w$::jsonb) as d(slug text, html text)
)
update authors a
   set works_html = d.html
  from data d
  join entries e on e.slug = d.slug and e.locale = 'en'
 where a.id = e.author_id and a.works_html = '';

update entries
   set summary_points = summary_points || array[$w$Sovereignty undermines human rights.$w$]
 where slug = 'current-global-debates-about-human-rights' and locale = 'en'
   and cardinality(summary_points) = 5
   and summary_points[5] = $w$Human rights cannot solve large-scale worldwide problems.$w$;
